# The campaign machine's parameters (design/CAMPAIGN.md section 2). ffi/campaign.sh
# sources this file; edit it to run the campaign on another machine. Values already
# set in the environment win.
#
# Reference machine (owner, 2026-09-26): Intel Core i9-7900X, 10 cores / 20 threads,
# one socket. Linux usually numbers the first thread of each core 0-9 and the SMT
# siblings 10-19; campaign.sh checks the sibling layout from sysfs, so a different
# numbering is caught, not silently accepted.
#
#   core 0     OS and the runner (with its sibling)
#   cores 1-4  CLIENT (the measured process)
#   cores 5-8  SERVER (the RPC server)
#   core 9     spare
#
# With SMT on, the siblings of CLIENT and SERVER cores (11-14, 15-18) are left idle:
# isolate them with the measured CPUs and do not schedule on them.

AK_MACHINE_NAME="${AK_MACHINE_NAME:-i9-7900X}"
AK_CPU_CLIENT="${AK_CPU_CLIENT:-1-4}"
AK_CPU_SERVER="${AK_CPU_SERVER:-5-8}"
# CAMPAIGN req 4 (R-H34): set sizes are fixed for the whole campaign.
AK_SET_SIZE="${AK_SET_SIZE:-4}"
